Task: The ancient Magic Orb needs its energy level to be protected from direct manipulation. Implement encapsulation by making the `_energyLevel` field private and ensure it can only be modified or read through public methods (`charge`, `discharge`, `getEnergyLevel`).

Submitted code:
```
class MagicOrb {
  // 1. Declare the private field
  #energyLevel;

  constructor(initialEnergy) {
    // 2. Initialize and clamp the private energy level
    this.#energyLevel = Math.min(100, Math.max(0, initialEnergy));
  }

  // 3. Implement charging logic with a cap
  charge(amount) {
    if (amount < 0) return "Amount must be positive.";
    this.#energyLevel = Math.min(100, this.#energyLevel + amount);
  }

  // 4. Implement discharging logic with a floor
  discharge(amount) {
    if (amount < 0) return "Amount must be positive.";
    this.#energyLevel = Math.max(0, this.#energyLevel - amount);
  }

  // 5. Provide a safe way to read the value
  getEnergyLevel() {
    return this.#energyLevel;
  }
}

// --- Example Usage ---
const orb = new MagicOrb(50);
console.log(orb.getEnergyLevel()); // 50

orb.charge(30);
console.log(orb.getEnergyLevel()); // 80

orb.discharge(90);
console.log(orb.getEnergyLevel()); // 0 (Capped at minimum)
```

